Falsifies `socket_contract::verification::a_listen_grant_admits_exactly_its_range`.

The defect: `grant_allows` drops its `lo != 0` test, the guard that makes a word with no listen
half grant nothing. `NO_LISTEN_GRANT` then reads as the range 0 to 0, and port 0 passes the
authority check under no grant at all.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `grant_allows`, with a low bound of 0 and port 0.

diff --git a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@
 pub const fn grant_allows(grant: u64, port: u16) -> bool {
     let lo = (grant & 0xffff) as u16;
     let hi = ((grant >> 16) & 0xffff) as u16;
-    lo != 0 && port >= lo && port <= hi
+    port >= lo && port <= hi
 }
 
